  'World Religions introduces students to major religious traditions, Indigenous and diasporic religious worlds, new religious movements, nonreligion, and cross-tradition themes through academic methods. Students study texts, rituals, ethics, material culture, social power, migration, media, and contemporary public life while learning that traditions are internally diverse, historically changing, and never reducible to a list of beliefs.',
  $wreljson${"slug": "world-religions", "title": "World Religions", "description": "World Religions introduces students to major religious traditions, Indigenous and diasporic religious worlds, new religious movements, nonreligion, and cross-tradition themes through academic methods. Students study texts, rituals, ethics, material culture, social power, migration, media, and contemporary public life while learning that traditions are internally diverse, historically changing, and never reducible to a list of beliefs.", "topics": [{"id": "777ad784-ece5-431f-b75a-0c027a2261b6", "type": "topic", "title": "World Religions as a Category: Map, Method, and Critique", "description": "This section builds the conceptual and factual depth needed for the module while keeping comparison responsible, evidence-based, and attentive to lived practice.", "children": [{"id": "c343b009-5dc9-4cb5-b34c-d9c2dd8ce872", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Why use the category?", "children": [{"id": "30dc290c-9079-4a29-93d1-745ee7991956", "type": "concept", "title": "Survey logic"}, {"id": "6467bc6b-0300-4847-bb35-744e8f55a1e5", "type": "concept", "title": "Pedagogical usefulness"}, {"id": "6c99a796-fbaf-4ec3-b405-73edd94980a0", "type": "concept", "title": "Limits of neat traditions"}], "description": "Students learn that the category can help organize a broad field, but it is not a neutral description of reality."}, {"id": "7159d1cd-3cf7-4bf1-8325-205fa9b346c3", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Critiques of the world religions paradigm", "children": [{"id": "e6f0048e-522f-4a28-ad8a-5c9f9ac23e1d", "type": "concept", "title": "Eurocentrism"}, {"id": "f9bb31c7-e74f-47d5-9849-a43ccbab671c", "type": "concept", "title": "Protestant model of religion"}, {"id": "115458a2-9e82-470c-abaa-7df86120a1fc", "type": "concept", "title": "Power and classification"}], "description": "Students see how the category can privilege large, textual, institutionally visible traditions and marginalize local or Indigenous practices."}, {"id": "2c740f69-9b79-4cbd-9902-e5a7aec97861", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Responsible comparison", "children": [{"id": "baf753f4-9cdf-4a0f-87e2-422f7e42c3a1", "type": "concept", "title": "Specific cases"}, {"id": "a3df1ad2-7445-4870-ae2e-c910482479d3", "type": "concept", "title": "Internal diversity"}, {"id": "68e99785-1842-4a7e-bb1d-37d5ed55e2bc", "type": "concept", "title": "Comparison with caveats"}], "description": "The course begins with humility about scale, translation, evidence, and the danger of flattening traditions."}]}, {"id": "63930ee3-0ea8-4990-b82d-3e100d6cafa0", "type": "topic", "title": "Tools for Comparing Religions: Myth, Ritual, Text, Ethics, Experience, and Community", "description": "This section builds the conceptual and factual depth needed for the module while keeping comparison responsible, evidence-based, and attentive to lived practice.", "children": [{"id": "afea2221-1fe3-45cb-920c-253d427fd08a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Myth and narrative", "children": [{"id": "11442a9c-52be-4385-913d-82518aad7fd5", "type": "concept", "title": "Cosmogony"}, {"id": "5498d9ab-0854-4e2e-b341-6812e83430cf", "type": "concept", "title": "Hero and ancestor stories"}, {"id": "a01b26a0-20a0-49ce-bc58-534eec6bf958", "type": "concept", "title": "Ritual retelling"}], "description": "Students learn to read sacred stories as meaning-making narratives, not simply as false claims or literal history."}, {"id": "53db2315-62ec-4d0e-b788-c4473a76df9d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Ritual and practice", "children": [{"id": "5237e034-8608-468d-9c49-933033efd573", "type": "concept", "title": "Rites of passage"}, {"id": "297123dd-47c1-44cc-8bc3-66923c7e7e2a", "type": "concept", "title": "Purity and sacrifice"}, {"id": "c542af1c-2c1e-4df6-98bd-f20d82233157", "type": "concept", "title": "Pilgrimage and festival"}], "description": "The point is to notice what people do with bodies, objects, calendars, food, sound, pilgrimage, and repeated action."}, {"id": "561a30fb-a199-484e-b243-d77280e4e339", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Texts, ethics, and experience", "children": [{"id": "c5115321-067d-4392-b1b7-9c69ceefecbe", "type": "concept", "title": "Canon and interpretation"}, {"id": "43ed4879-58a9-4352-a8b0-57feaa1ec48a", "type": "concept", "title": "Virtue, law, compassion"}, {"id": "158503eb-400b-4701-9c13-83e74598875d", "type": "concept", "title": "Mysticism and conversion"}], "description": "Students build tools for comparing scripture, commentary, moral reasoning, mystical experience, and community authority."}]}, {"id": "be1b480d-17e8-4767-9810-8f644eae987b", "type": "topic", "title": "Indigenous, Oral, and Land-Based Traditions", "description": "This section builds the conceptual and factual depth needed for the module while keeping comparison responsible, evidence-based, and attentive to lived practice.", "children": [{"id": "06562a6e-eb2f-42f2-87c8-1b91f750b95d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Land and sacred geography", "children": [{"id": "154ce1ee-7b86-42f4-bdd3-b5d70aebda27", "type": "concept", "title": "Sacred sites"}, {"id": "1c23ec54-a4a6-4125-908d-9c842edc18ed", "type": "concept", "title": "Seasonal ceremony"}, {"id": "7b4aa43a-a064-4aa5-9af0-59ba672bdd06", "type": "concept", "title": "Land and law"}], "description": "Students learn why place, ecology, ancestors, and sovereignty are often inseparable in Indigenous traditions."}, {"id": "216009c2-b0a1-47e0-a2d0-3ec37b78637a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Oral tradition and memory", "children": [{"id": "61308776-dcd3-4b49-8fbe-f087b190f521", "type": "concept", "title": "Story cycles"}, {"id": "ec2f176e-8b01-469c-b7c5-6b1f7bce48cd", "type": "concept", "title": "Elders and authority"}, {"id": "4f557c44-f417-4dc0-8312-63759d635cf7", "type": "concept", "title": "Performance and memory"}], "description": "The goal is to understand oral transmission as rigorous cultural knowledge, not as an inferior substitute for text."}, {"id": "9df954f6-c212-42c2-93df-5a55a07ab590", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Colonialism and resilience", "children": [{"id": "8348ad53-f32d-42b9-a87b-4f3b9a7ba35c", "type": "concept", "title": "Missionization"}, {"id": "8c0fae20-2ed6-4628-81d9-475ebebe5249", "type": "concept", "title": "Boarding schools"}, {"id": "20e7fc01-01c6-47c1-881f-77dd0b787639", "type": "concept", "title": "Cultural renewal"}], "description": "Students examine suppression, adaptation, repatriation, revitalization, and Indigenous religious freedom."}]}, {"id": "e7ab01ec-52ee-40b2-85f9-f987b7e429f2", "type": "topic", "title": "African and African Diasporic Religions", "description": "This section builds the conceptual and factual depth needed for the module while keeping comparison responsible, evidence-based, and attentive to lived practice.", "children": [{"id": "673ce4b2-3893-4e99-8f1f-aec3413debc6", "type": "subtopic", "title": "African religious worlds", "children": [{"id": "b487f426-86d4-49f9-a813-3cfd938eb90b", "type": "concept", "title": "Yoruba orisha"}, {"id": "25554b7d-ebe0-4f91-9b7f-3ef3e7ad94ad", "type": "concept", "title": "Ancestors"}, {"id": "25c6c517-6c8f-4a17-b2d3-cb1b81838a12", "type": "concept", "title": "Divination and healing"}], "description": "Students study divination, ancestors, spirits, healing, kingship, sacrifice, and community in selected African contexts."}, {"id": "6f14d3e6-eea0-4c8b-9bb7-b86b8054bf03", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Diaspora formation", "children": [{"id": "c01ca29e-a4d5-4346-8a9e-668fa3f76399", "type": "concept", "title": "Vodun"}, {"id": "0c699231-3ffc-448a-962d-22569e380273", "type": "concept", "title": "Candomble"}, {"id": "cd5feca1-3455-4901-afe9-dc545008dcbe", "type": "concept", "title": "Santeria/Lucumi"}], "description": "Students trace how enslaved and displaced peoples preserved, adapted, and re-created traditions across the Atlantic."}, {"id": "c6360ca4-8ecd-4589-8e67-1613fc140c36", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Race, resistance, and modern identity", "children": [{"id": "a9d82c81-3d4d-45a3-8cf3-4e54853ffafd", "type": "concept", "title": "Rastafari"}, {"id": "a9e3b13e-d8d6-4e36-a6f3-68cad146b076", "type": "concept", "title": "Black Atlantic"}, {"id": "6db3e884-e65f-4c66-9fe3-ef7e5959c73a", "type": "concept", "title": "Music and ritual memory"}], "description": "The section shows how religion has supported survival, resistance, art, politics, and identity."}]}, {"id": "3110d6c1-eb09-4e1b-b3f1-5a45f7a5483b", "type": "topic", "title": "Hindu Traditions", "description": "This section builds the conceptual and factual depth needed for the module while keeping comparison responsible, evidence-based, and attentive to lived practice.", "children": [{"id": "3b294188-8e27-4c6a-9eef-30c049d9c162", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Texts and philosophical worlds", "children": [{"id": "67247bd8-bbaa-4915-bfff-51f56850b6d0", "type": "concept", "title": "Dharma"}, {"id": "c7c54e52-537d-4b80-929e-29b85efea0b1", "type": "concept", "title": "Karma and samsara"}, {"id": "10483f7c-8aaa-4639-9621-3b4add6412bd", "type": "concept", "title": "Moksha"}], "description": "Students encounter Vedas, Upanishads, epics, Puranas, and philosophical ideas without reducing Hinduism to a single doctrine."}, {"id": "c1390f94-627e-4457-8a1c-16b7c7b3ca62", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Practice and devotion", "children": [{"id": "efe25f62-7490-4cb2-be65-385fc3a37478", "type": "concept", "title": "Puja"}, {"id": "599c4c51-1d2d-4575-9587-68712cee804d", "type": "concept", "title": "Bhakti poetry"}, {"id": "a64a9cca-c4aa-44a0-8377-49ff059bdef2", "type": "concept", "title": "Temple and home rituals"}], "description": "Students learn how puja, bhakti, pilgrimage, festivals, temples, image worship, and household practice structure Hindu life."}, {"id": "9ae90685-cc74-4a22-8634-04cf6a0e2abb", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Society and modernity", "children": [{"id": "222cdeba-b417-4b38-b06c-b0b68ea63de0", "type": "concept", "title": "Caste and critique"}, {"id": "fa2d2249-c80d-4cde-874a-136b