litics"}], "description": "The section explores meditation movements, engaged Buddhism, nationalism, diaspora, and Western adaptations."}]}, {"id": "fc43c54c-5aa6-40a9-95fb-54fcc0182e14", "type": "topic", "title": "Jain and Sikh Traditions", "description": "This section builds the conceptual and factual depth needed for the module while keeping comparison responsible, evidence-based, and attentive to lived practice.", "children": [{"id": "8d2ff60c-e1d2-4a17-b3c7-37365990c6bd", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Jain traditions", "children": [{"id": "81b621c2-ad92-44e0-ad81-5a9590853a54", "type": "concept", "title": "Nonviolence"}, {"id": "b1ba88b2-8e8b-42ba-91e5-20e87ef57fa1", "type": "concept", "title": "Anekantavada"}, {"id": "dad00af4-6490-4443-a806-bf9b0b78b5cb", "type": "concept", "title": "Monastic and lay life"}], "description": "Students study ahimsa, karma, asceticism, lay ethics, Tirthankaras, community, and liberation."}, {"id": "dbda2f7e-171d-433c-8383-e9ac0bb65eb1", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Sikh traditions", "children": [{"id": "6959e5a5-d268-46d0-879b-5ef404a26d86", "type": "concept", "title": "Guru Granth Sahib"}, {"id": "a73b8b50-4c5a-4f74-b18e-e0d4d4b13ce3", "type": "concept", "title": "Langar"}, {"id": "fa4fdad9-e2a1-444c-a90b-befed9028164", "type": "concept", "title": "Khalsa identity"}], "description": "Students learn about Guru Nanak, the Gurus, Guru Granth Sahib, sangat, langar, Khalsa, and service."}, {"id": "d15b6ae9-ffc4-4d7f-afb9-d77d02dfabc5", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Ethics and diaspora", "children": [{"id": "ee42262c-ec5a-4f31-9ad9-66edf364b8e4", "type": "concept", "title": "Food ethics"}, {"id": "cb44c01c-7ef8-4cb9-bc87-cb4e6a17d229", "type": "concept", "title": "Seva"}, {"id": "96a3f7ed-7719-4251-9fc0-cce6ba91bca3", "type": "concept", "title": "Diaspora communities"}], "description": "The section connects religious practice to vegetarianism, service, identity, diaspora, and public visibility."}]}, {"id": "5d2535bb-00e8-4f2d-995d-faa4bb2da91b", "type": "topic", "title": "Chinese and East Asian Traditions: Confucianism, Daoism, Shinto, and Popular Religion", "description": "This section builds the conceptual and factual depth needed for the module while keeping comparison responsible, evidence-based, and attentive to lived practice.", "children": [{"id": "f55bc9bc-efe6-4316-8ddb-fe2cd3524454", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Confucian traditions", "children": [{"id": "344013a3-ea9c-4789-b122-a4ce5f970ff7", "type": "concept", "title": "Ren and li"}, {"id": "c78761f3-bafd-4e76-b1fd-f1248747ebfe", "type": "concept", "title": "Ancestor rites"}, {"id": "ee9dc269-7b0d-422c-b6ff-bcadda716e97", "type": "concept", "title": "Civil service and learning"}], "description": "Students analyze ritual, family, education, ethics, hierarchy, cultivation, and statecraft."}, {"id": "d94903bf-79b1-4f05-b218-f181ab7d425c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Daoism and Chinese popular religion", "children": [{"id": "af3a9782-f1bb-41cc-8a34-440a28276e29", "type": "concept", "title": "Dao and wuwei"}, {"id": "218daaf3-edd3-410c-84e7-4fab5c2ea510", "type": "concept", "title": "Ritual registers"}, {"id": "ae7b7818-df68-41c9-8cb7-e3c4893e43a7", "type": "concept", "title": "Local deities"}], "description": "Students study Dao, ritual specialists, temples, immortality, cosmology, gods, ancestors, and local cults."}, {"id": "263787aa-0d0b-48da-8fd7-3d154ac8a731", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Shinto and Japanese religious life", "children": [{"id": "23fc6254-86af-4395-8a7c-d17a50bb4846", "type": "concept", "title": "Kami"}, {"id": "3138a3d2-650c-401c-a39b-4bbb75e14b5a", "type": "concept", "title": "Matsuri"}, {"id": "17c4c463-e801-4e55-b9b8-6fe196931aae", "type": "concept", "title": "State Shinto debates"}], "description": "Students learn shrine practice, kami, purification, festivals, Buddhism-Shinto interaction, and modern public religion."}]}, {"id": "12cf063c-811c-468a-8211-2ac433fd31c6", "type": "topic", "title": "Judaism", "description": "This section builds the conceptual and factual depth needed for the module while keeping comparison responsible, evidence-based, and attentive to lived practice.", "children": [{"id": "8bd0ce17-3ca0-49c3-9c5e-f0f5a4f2bfa3", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Text, law, and interpretation", "children": [{"id": "51d1134f-1e38-4f23-8a49-b6e83e413825", "type": "concept", "title": "Covenant"}, {"id": "db8cf4aa-f44b-44d6-8603-cce2e7255fb4", "type": "concept", "title": "Rabbinic tradition"}, {"id": "ea8dec25-1b89-454d-a7a5-8278b5b401ed", "type": "concept", "title": "Interpretive debate"}], "description": "Students learn how Torah, Tanakh, Talmud, midrash, halakhah, and commentary shape Jewish life."}, {"id": "a2d4c5e2-e285-44d0-82a6-2c5f741b2b19", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Ritual calendar and community", "children": [{"id": "a42ff84b-ca8f-42ba-b797-60a8f2a08706", "type": "concept", "title": "Shabbat"}, {"id": "d358de19-01fd-4830-bcf9-34691254cf33", "type": "concept", "title": "Passover"}, {"id": "87902fc9-6c20-4433-8879-1ec63f961584", "type": "concept", "title": "Kashrut"}], "description": "The section studies Sabbath, festivals, lifecycle rituals, synagogue, home practice, and food laws."}, {"id": "a29c2d33-e8b3-4872-a16b-d6b8ddfe7eab", "type": "subtopic", "title": "History, diaspora, and modern Jewish identities", "children": [{"id": "9f3eb79e-7ee2-4a24-8bb9-ace329aa0900", "type": "concept", "title": "Diaspora"}, {"id": "ab21ca65-3e4b-4b9f-91bf-7f02e2021e72", "type": "concept", "title": "Holocaust memory"}, {"id": "f782a301-156a-4eac-a897-82c8bfa6dca2", "type": "concept", "title": "Modern movements"}], "description": "Students examine exile, diaspora, memory, emancipation, antisemitism, Zionism, denominational diversity, and contemporary life."}]}, {"id": "3e812d49-7954-4e91-a84f-bd1535126ff1", "type": "topic", "title": "Christianity", "description": "This section builds the conceptual and factual depth needed for the module while keeping comparison responsible, evidence-based, and attentive to lived practice.", "children": [{"id": "0715df6b-7087-41a8-9549-a080c97ab2f0", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Origins and scripture", "children": [{"id": "038554b3-465a-431b-aca8-8e904f08c16e", "type": "concept", "title": "Gospels and Paul"}, {"id": "de8957a0-5835-4b28-a9f3-b34aebd99e84", "type": "concept", "title": "Canon formation"}, {"id": "d2d07649-78f1-4fc4-8f08-7e6f99baffd8", "type": "concept", "title": "Creeds and councils"}], "description": "Students study Jesus movements, New Testament contexts, canon, early church, creeds, and interpretation."}, {"id": "876883eb-1d1e-4129-a243-bdae2ea0cd6a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Institutions, ritual, and reform", "children": [{"id": "7ad11bbe-028a-4acd-84f3-35e2e4b7bc16", "type": "concept", "title": "Baptism and Eucharist"}, {"id": "39db91a7-a470-4d2f-9f5d-69c91d1c342b", "type": "concept", "title": "Monastic life"}, {"id": "e87290a1-63eb-44fc-81cc-88e012a3b851", "type": "concept", "title": "Reformation"}], "description": "The section follows sacraments, church structures, monasticism, Orthodoxy, Catholicism, Protestant reform, and modern denominations."}, {"id": "ddde8c3d-32f3-4071-aa8d-51abbba36bc3", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Global Christianity", "children": [{"id": "ddd3f2a8-e0c3-4503-95ac-d9beca67fb9d", "type": "concept", "title": "Pentecostal movements"}, {"id": "5e8195da-8d40-42bc-8f0c-d75f3dd53717", "type": "concept", "title": "Liberation theology"}, {"id": "f0f0e84a-7c75-4342-83b6-7b7037efc07e", "type": "concept", "title": "Postcolonial Christianity"}], "description": "Students examine missions, colonialism, Pentecostalism, liberation theology, migration, and Christianity in Africa, Asia, and Latin America."}]}, {"id": "a75dc926-8fab-4db1-8507-ad46ec96dfcd", "type": "topic", "title": "Islam", "description": "This section builds the conceptual and factual depth needed for the module while keeping comparison responsible, evidence-based, and attentive to lived practice.